f. Training and programs to enhance the capability and competence of personnel and staff, including those detailed with the CENTER;

g. Information dissemination and campaign to the public on tax credit and duty drawback schemes, policies and issues.

h. Networking with other government agencies, International Organizations and private sector groups and entities in connection with tax credit and duty drawback matters;

i. Such other activities and programs, as may be deemed appropriate by the Executive Committee, to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of the CENTER including but not limited to allowances, overtime pays, and hazard pays to its members and staff including employees of other government agencies assigned to the CENTER;

SECTION 3. The Executive Committee of the CENTER shall be composed of representatives from the following agencies:

